GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_DesignTradeoffs> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_DesignTradeoffs> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#DesignTradeoffs> ;
    narr:childCount "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "6da9891f90cce25018457b985bfc79ca59c4b513" ;
    narr:narration """This region holds a single, fully recorded trade-off: [one bundle per run per person rather than one message per skill](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2), with the bundle [closing when the run closes, late skills waiting for the next run](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4). The rejected alternative is kept expandable alongside the verdict — [per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing, which moves the ordering problem onto the reader](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5). The choice was contested and the contest is in the record: [a pushback on the batching window, held against](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3), relayed through the same ruling. The parent frame states the aim as [shielding recipients from fragmentation](narr:Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling).""" ;
    narr:reaction """Nothing moved here — the same four children underlie this digest and the prior narration still holds: the [one-bundle-per-run verdict](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2), the [close-of-run rule](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4), the [rejected per-skill alternative](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5), and the [held pushback](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3) are unchanged. If anything, the contest reads slightly sharper on re-narration: the pushback is signed by its challenger, so the held position and the dissent are both attributable in the record.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "we route every reaction through one bundle per run per person, not one\n> message per skill — a person should get one thing to read, not four" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Tanya held: the bundle closes when\nthe run closes, and a skill that misses the close waits for the next run rather\nthan sending on its own." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The alternative considered and rejected was per-skill\ndelivery with client-side collapsing, which moves the ordering problem onto the\nreader." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Tina pushed back on the batching window" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The batching window was contested — a pushback on when the bundle closes, held against rather than resolved by argument" ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The rejected alternative remains on record: per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing, trading server-side bundling for reader-side ordering" ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:writer "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:nitro" .
}